From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 02:17:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 028/260] [ae-patch] Preselect and tag the recommended merge
 method on a pull request card

Reid asked on 2026-09-28, from a screenshot of the chat card's confirm step
("Squash and merge #60 into main?"), that the step say which method to use,
select it by default, and keep the other selectable. The confirm step always
opened on squash, which is wrong when a pull request promotes one long-lived
branch into another (dev into main): a squash puts a commit on the base that
the head never gets, and the next promotion conflicts.

omnigent-ae's server now decides (recommend_merge_method in
ae_omni_policies.prs) and adds recommended_method and recommended_reason to
the card's merge block; default_method follows the recommendation. ConfirmMerge
opens on the recommended method, its segment carries a small muted
"Recommended" pill and the reason as its title, and the reason is one muted
line under the question. The question still follows the selected method, and
picking the other method still merges with it. A card without the fields (an
older server) behaves exactly as before.

Only P12's own files change: AePrCards.tsx, AePrCards.test.tsx and the card
type in lib/aePrs.ts; no upstream file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
